"Sylvain of Saltport was never a man; he was a persona worn by a shapeshifting slime named Syl."
"The gold-rank elf adventurer Syl is that same slime, a tier-five monster posing as an elf."
"A class crystal starts to work once its settlement has counted as a city for a full day."
"The guild, the dwarves and the elves keep the Artificer profession quietly unadvertised."
"The deepstone signing bonus is really hazard pay, for gathering crews often die."
"Keldenar was reborn from another world, and his golems quietly judge guild newcomers."
"The ghost caretaker of the demon labyrinth raises its difficulty for anyone who returns."
"A god made the demon labyrinth a trial ground and claims the souls of all who die there."
